Load BigQuery from bigquery-adbc instead of dbt's CDN

A release build compiles in the URL, version and SHA-256 of its release's library, and dbt's own
downloader fetches and verifies it into dbt's cache under the name bigquery_adbc. Any other build
loads the library in lib/bigquery-adbc/ beside the binary. Neither reads stock dbt's lib/dbt/ for
BigQuery, so an install sharing a prefix with stock dbt cannot pick up dbt's driver, or replace it.

BIGQUERY_ADBC_USE_DBT_DRIVER=1 resolves BigQuery exactly as stock dbt does, including its Foundry
opt-in. The two drivers are cached under different names, so runs can switch back and forth.

